From: HeDo <ldileo@digipa.it>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 18:57:29 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 3/5] OutStream::write<T> stores a value with memcpy

It stored the value through a T pointer into the byte buffer, at an offset that is not a
multiple of sizeof(T) once a 1 or 2 byte value or a string precedes it: an unaligned store,
undefined in C++ (UBSan: "store to misaligned address ... which requires 4 byte alignment").
memcpy of sizeof(T) bytes writes the same bytes, in host order as before, and the compiler turns
it into the same single store where the target allows it.
---
 include/corto/cstream.h | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/include/corto/cstream.h b/include/corto/cstream.h
index 71cf935..47ce22a 100644
--- a/include/corto/cstream.h
+++ b/include/corto/cstream.h
@@ -64,7 +64,7 @@ public:
 
 	template<class T> void write(T c) {
 		uchar *pos = grow(sizeof(T));
-		*(T *)pos = c;
+		memcpy(pos, &c, sizeof(T));
 	}
 	template<class T> void writeArray(int count, T *c) {
 		push(c, count*sizeof(T));
